<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  ManualDrive ADAS verification scenario 10_manualdrive_adas / md_sng_traffic_light
  (req-vd-ad:REQ-AD-031 step b, vd-func:FUNC-079; slug md-sng-traffic-light-stop).
  Added 2026-08-05 (phase D warm-up: the second phase-C slug whose implementation
  was complete and whose only missing piece was a stimulus).

  Road: fabriksgatan_traffic_lights.xodr, the SAME road and the SAME persistent-red
  signal controller the VirtualDriver's own red_hold asset uses (03_traffic_signals).
  Reusing it is the point: step b specifies the manual stop as "the same stop-line
  basis as the VD case", and comparability is what makes that claim checkable rather
  than merely asserted.

  ============================================================================
  WHAT THIS RUN CLOSES, AND WHY IT NEEDED A **JUNCTION** ROAD
  ============================================================================
  Phase C confirmed StopYieldSignAware works for a routeless ManualDrive ego, but
  recorded the confirmation's scope honestly (design §12): ONE policy, on ONE
  STRAIGHT road. Two things were left untested and both are here.

  (1) TrafficLightAware itself. It is a different policy with its own cross-frame
      latches; "the other one worked" is not evidence about it.

  (2) THE BRANCH. Both policies find their signal by walking forward from the ego's
      own Position via RouteSignalScan's `pos.CopyRoute(ego->pos_)`, and a
      ManualDrive ego has NO Route to copy. On a straight road that is invisible -
      there is only one way forward, so route-following and straight-most walking
      agree. Road 3 here feeds junction 4 through THREE connecting roads (11 / 12 /
      13), so the walk has to actually choose, and the choice is made by
      MoveAlongS(..., HEADING_DIRECTION, true) picking the straight-most connection
      rather than by any route. That is the untested behaviour, and this is the
      geometry that exercises it.

  Deliberately NO RoutingAction, unlike red_hold.xosc. Adding one would hand the
  scan a route to copy and destroy the very thing this scenario exists to measure.
  A human driver has no assigned route, so its absence is also the honest model.

  Ego drives itself: steering stays 0 for the whole run (profiles/acc_ops_engage.json)
  and road 3's planView is a paramPoly3 whose curvature coefficients are ~1e-18,
  i.e. a straight line - so zero steering keeps the ego in lane -1 all the way to
  the signal. This scenario would NOT be sound on a curved approach: the ego would
  drift out of its lane and the stop would be measured somewhere the road never
  put it.

  Signal at s=109 on road 3, ego released at s=11 -> ~98 m of approach at 13.889 m/s
  (~7 s), inside a 25 s run with room for the stop AND the hold to be measured as
  settled values. The light never turns green, so the hold is the terminal state and
  nothing has to be timed against a phase change.
-->
<OpenSCENARIO>
   <FileHeader revMajor="1" revMinor="3" date="2026-08-05T00:00:00"
               description="ManualDrive ADAS verification: ACC Stop-and-Go stops at a red light when the traffic light is a configured target" author="GT_esmini"/>
   <ParameterDeclarations>
      <ParameterDeclaration name="EgoSpeed" parameterType="double" value="13.889"/>
   </ParameterDeclarations>
   <CatalogLocations/>
   <RoadNetwork>
      <LogicFile filepath="../../../xodr/fabriksgatan_traffic_lights.xodr"/>
      <TrafficSignals>
         <TrafficSignalController name="MainController" delay="0">
            <Phase name="red" duration="60">
               <TrafficSignalState trafficSignalId="1" state="on;off;off"/>
               <TrafficSignalState trafficSignalId="2" state="off;on"/>
               <TrafficSignalState trafficSignalId="3" state="off;on"/>
            </Phase>
         </TrafficSignalController>
      </TrafficSignals>
   </RoadNetwork>
   <Entities>
      <ScenarioObject name="Ego">
         <Vehicle name="car_white" vehicleCategory="car" model3d="../../../models/car_white.osgb">
            <BoundingBox>
               <Center x="1.4" y="0.0" z="0.9"/>
               <Dimensions width="2.0" length="5.0" height="1.8"/>
            </BoundingBox>
            <Performance maxSpeed="69" maxDeceleration="30" maxAcceleration="10"/>
            <Axles>
               <FrontAxle maxSteering="30" wheelDiameter="0.8" trackWidth="1.68" positionX="2.98" positionZ="0.4"/>
               <RearAxle maxSteering="30" wheelDiameter="0.8" trackWidth="1.68" positionX="0" positionZ="0.4"/>
            </Axles>
            <Properties>
               <Property name="model_id" value="0"/>
               <Property name="scaleMode" value="ModelToBB"/>
            </Properties>
         </Vehicle>
         <ObjectController>
            <Controller name="ManualDriveController">
               <Properties>
                  <Property name="esminiController" value="ManualDriveController"/>
                  <Property name="ConfigFile" value="manual_drive_headless_stub.json"/>
               </Properties>
            </Controller>
         </ObjectController>
      </ScenarioObject>
   </Entities>
   <Storyboard>
      <Init>
         <Actions>
            <Private entityRef="Ego">
               <PrivateAction>
                  <TeleportAction>
                     <Position><LanePosition roadId="3" laneId="-1" offset="0" s="11"/></Position>
                  </TeleportAction>
               </PrivateAction>
               <PrivateAction>
                  <LongitudinalAction>
                     <SpeedAction>
                        <SpeedActionDynamics dynamicsShape="step" value="0" dynamicsDimension="time"/>
                        <SpeedActionTarget><AbsoluteTargetSpeed value="$EgoSpeed"/></SpeedActionTarget>
                     </SpeedAction>
                  </LongitudinalAction>
               </PrivateAction>
               <PrivateAction>
                  <ControllerAction>
                     <ActivateControllerAction objectControllerRef="ManualDriveController" lateral="true" longitudinal="true"/>
                  </ControllerAction>
               </PrivateAction>
            </Private>
         </Actions>
      </Init>
      <Story name="SngTrafficLightStory">
         <Act name="SngTrafficLightAct">
            <ManeuverGroup maximumExecutionCount="1" name="EgoSequence">
               <Actors selectTriggeringEntities="false"><EntityRef entityRef="Ego"/></Actors>
            </ManeuverGroup>
            <StartTrigger>
               <ConditionGroup>
                  <Condition name="ActStart" delay="0" conditionEdge="none">
                     <ByValueCondition><SimulationTimeCondition value="0" rule="greaterThan"/></ByValueCondition>
                  </Condition>
               </ConditionGroup>
            </StartTrigger>
         </Act>
      </Story>
      <StopTrigger>
         <ConditionGroup>
            <Condition name="StopCondition" delay="0" conditionEdge="rising">
               <ByValueCondition><SimulationTimeCondition value="25" rule="greaterThan"/></ByValueCondition>
            </Condition>
         </ConditionGroup>
      </StopTrigger>
   </Storyboard>
</OpenSCENARIO>
